# Normal webhook bodies and exact durable completion share one transaction.
register_gate "tests/test_atomic_delivery_finalize.py" "ATOMIC DELIVERY FINALIZE GATE: PASS" "one-transaction delivery finalization and commit-ACK recovery" "the real DeliveryStore wrapper and make_db_processor pass an execution-only exact-generation capability that is popped before handlers; a normal body stages finish as its final SQL and commits once; a lost COMMIT response or typed cancellation resolves committed without replay; queued/failed, ABA, and resolver failures preserve the original error; pre-stage failures retain exact release; atomic generation-fence no-ops converge on the same finalize; direct and early-noop callers retain separate-finish compatibility, while durable fanout carries the exact capability into its own checkpoint/finalize protocol" "a server-side committed webhook cannot be replayed merely because its COMMIT ACK disappeared, and a stale lease cannot finalize or release a successor generation"
